# N2/P11 Results - Frozen-Tree Specialized Telemetry

## Status

P11 is complete. The P8/P9/P10 dispatch policy, `0.80` cutoff, P6 folding backend, and evaluation corpora were held fixed. P11 changed only telemetry implementation by compiling the already-frozen annotate decision into a threshold-aware construction path.

Mandatory decision invariance passed on **332/332** frozen policy cases: 188 training, 98 validation, 36 Gate-P evaluation, and 10 natural evaluation cases. Fresh fuzz passed **1000/1000**.

P11 reproduces P10's `edge_count`, `binary_nodes`, `reuse_edge_events`, `pair_repeat_excess`, the predicate `max_pair_shells >= 5`, and final annotate/bypass decision. It intentionally does not compute P10's unused bypass-branch depth/density features.

## Gate-P primary endpoint

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P11 / direct, source-inclusive | **1.043490x** | **0.974046-1.093383** | **1.004381x** | 2/36 |
| P11 / P10, source-inclusive | **0.969953x** | **0.963118-0.977106** | **0.969859x** | 33/36 |
| P11 / direct, source build | **1.364523x** | **1.334510-1.392409** | **1.377555x** | 0/36 |
| P11 / P10, source build | **0.899800x** | **0.892271-0.907540** | **0.899226x** | 36/36 |
| P11 / direct, selected compiler | **0.967099x** | **0.861371-1.047296** | **0.822394x** | 8/36 |

The preregistered **direct-crossover criterion failed**. P11 is about **4.3% slower than direct** case-balanced, and the confidence interval crosses 1. The workload-weighted result is only **0.44% above direct**, effectively near parity but not a preregistered win.

The preregistered **specialized-telemetry engineering criterion passed**: P11/P10 source build is **0.899800x**, P11/P10 source-inclusive is **0.969953x**, and the latter's complete 95% interval is below 1. P11 beat P10 source construction on all **36/36** Gate-P cases and source-inclusive on **33/36**.

Median-of-case-median Gate-P source construction was approximately **46.7 us direct**, **72.5 us P10**, and **65.7 us P11**. Corresponding whole-pipeline medians were approximately **229.9 us**, **262.1 us**, and **249.9 us**.

