## Dispatch and Boolean work

P11 made exactly the same final decisions as frozen P10/P8: **5/36** Gate-P cases annotated, all **5** consuming a fold, for **5** total consumed folds.

Relative to simultaneous always-P6 timing, 2 annotations were P6 wins, 3 were P6 losses, and 4 P6-winning cases were bypassed. This is unchanged policy behavior, not a P11 retuning result.

Because dispatch is invariant, Boolean work is the same selective mechanism as P8-P10:

- multiplications: **0.812451x direct**;
- pair terms: **0.570459x direct**;
- peak monomials: **0.978577x direct**;
- ANF nodes evaluated: **0.873553x direct**.

## Memory

Gate-P traced peak allocation was **0.993015x direct** and **0.985977x P10**. P11 removes the per-node depth bytearray and generic feature bookkeeping, but the five folded cases also materially alter downstream allocation, so this is a whole-pipeline measurement rather than isolated telemetry size.

## Natural EPFL control

P11 annotated **0/10** frozen natural cases and consumed **0 folds**. Natural results therefore remain strictly an abstention/overhead control.

| Comparison | Case-balanced geomean | 95% bootstrap CI | Workload-weighted | Wins |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| P11 / direct, source-inclusive | **1.005777x** | **0.997385-1.015090** | **0.996435x** | 4/10 |
| P11 / P10, source-inclusive | **0.987400x** | **0.971973-1.002578** | **0.994823x** | 7/10 |
| P11 / direct, source build | **1.378885x** | **1.207039-1.659587** | **1.282943x** | 0/10 |
| P11 / P10, source build | **0.926492x** | **0.865128-1.025622** | **0.986046x** | 9/10 |

Case-balanced natural source-inclusive overhead is about **0.58%**. The workload-weighted point estimate is slightly below direct, but with zero folds it is not a natural-folding speedup claim.

## Post-hoc diagnostic

Keeping P11's exact frozen dispatch decisions and measured compiler medians, but hypothetically replacing P11 source-build time by direct source-build time, gives **0.962603x direct case-balanced** and **0.878500x workload-weighted**. This is diagnostic only, not a measured implementation endpoint.

## Predeclared outcomes

- Gate-P direct-crossover PASS: **False**.
- Specialized-telemetry engineering success: **True**.

P11 therefore validates the implementation hypothesis that frozen-tree specialization can materially reduce telemetry cost, while leaving the stronger end-to-end direct crossover unresolved.
